{
  "rewrites": [
    {
      "source": "/:slug",
      "has": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "key": "user-agent",
          "value": "(?i).*(facebookexternalhit|WhatsApp|Twitterbot|LinkedInBot|Slackbot|Discordbot|TelegramBot|Pinterest|SkypeUriPreview|Applebot|redditbot|vkShare|W3C_Validator|Google-InspectionTool|bingbot|Googlebot-Image|googleweblight|GoogleOther).*"
        }
      ],
      "destination": "/api/og?slug=:slug"
    },
    {
      "source": "/:slug/registry",
      "destination": "/weddings/live_registry.html"
    },
    {
      "source": "/:slug/:page",
      "destination": "/index.html"
    },
    {
      "source": "/:slug",
      "destination": "/index.html"
    }
  ],
  "headers": [
    {
      "source": "/printess-theme.css",
      "headers": [
        {
          "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin",
          "value": "*"
        },
        {
          "key": "Cache-Control",
          "value": "public, max-age=300"
        },
        {
          "key": "Content-Type",
          "value": "text/css; charset=utf-8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "/(og-image|apple-touch-icon|favicon-32x32|favicon-16x16|favicon)\\.(png|ico)",
      "headers": [
        {
          "key": "Cache-Control",
          "value": "public, max-age=604800, immutable"
        },
        {
          "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin",
          "value": "*"
        },
        {
          "key": "X-Content-Type-Options",
          "value": "nosniff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ten templates and the runtime, kept out of the EDGE cache.",
      "comment2": "Cache-Control below is read by the browser; it says nothing about Vercel's own cache, so the edge applied its own default and held these files. A deploy would land on the origin and weddings.myplanning.ai would keep serving the previous copy - x-vercel-cache HIT with an age of 197s on a build that was already live. Four rounds of debugging were spent on code that was already correct.",
      "comment3": "CDN-Cache-Control is read by the edge and ignored by browsers, so this changes nothing for visitors. Narrow on purpose: these files are small, change often, and are the ones a deploy must land immediately. Everything else keeps the caching it has.",
      "source": "/(template-[a-z]+\\.html|site-runtime\\.js)",
      "headers": [
        {
          "key": "CDN-Cache-Control",
          "value": "no-store"
        },
        {
          "key": "Cache-Control",
          "value": "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "/(.*)",
      "headers": [
        {
          "key": "Cache-Control",
          "value": "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
        },
        {
          "key": "X-Content-Type-Options",
          "value": "nosniff"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
